  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A square loop <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>, mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and total resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is falling under gravity in a region of transverse non-uniform magnetic field given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is a positive constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;is the position of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;of the loop. If at some instant the speed of the loop is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>, then the total Lorentz&nbsp;force acting on the loop is</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0009083_Ques1_1..jpg\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 173px;\" /></p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
